<!-- <head> is ignored - only its children are copied into the output page head. -->
<!--
    Force-dark loader for the Oxygen WebHelp Responsive template (issue #173).

    Loading dark-mode.js pins data-wh-theme="dark" on the <html> element, so
    every published page renders in the template's dark theme regardless of the
    reader's browser preference or any earlier choice they made in the theme
    menu. The companion resources/dark-mode.css hides that menu.

    NOTE the deliberate absence of defer/async: this script must run before the
    first paint, otherwise the page renders light for a frame and then flips.
    (The GramFrame fragment beside this one IS deferred - it upgrades the DOM
    after load, which is the opposite requirement.)

    The bundle ships beside this fragment under resources/dark-mode.js; Oxygen's
    custom-resources fileset copies resources/** into the output at
    ${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/, so the src below mirrors
    the path convention the template's other custom scripts already use.

    Bind this fragment to the "webhelp.fragment.head" placeholder - the one that
    applies to ALL page types (welcome, topic, search results, index terms), not
    just topic pages. That placeholder is free: the GramFrame fragment occupies
    "webhelp.fragment.head.topic.page", and Oxygen binds one fragment per
    placeholder.
-->
<head xmlns:whc="http://www.oxygenxml.com/webhelp/components" whc:version="22.0">
    <script
        src="${oxygen-webhelp-assets-dir}/template/resources/dark-mode.js?buildId=${oxygen-webhelp-build-number}"></script>
</head>
